WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.651
A class in a world now gets its world ready first: World loading, then Start riding.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.992
The world downloads with its bytes counted, and stays on this device, so next time

00:00:14.992 --> 00:00:16.772
that step is done at once.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.940
Then the renderer from main builds the shaders and warms up the first frames off

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.419
screen, and Start riding takes focus.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.696
If the download stops, the card says where, and Try again picks up from the bytes

00:00:40.696 --> 00:00:41.954
already received.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:55.126
A browser without WebGPU or WebGL 2 rides the panorama: the plan, clock and bike

00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:56.491
work the same.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.261
The class over its world, and the load card, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.867
What the tests prove: the world downloads, resumes, is saved, and the ride waits for

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:20.944
Start riding.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
